body:
### Tested versions

- reproducible in Godot 4.6
- not reproducible in Godot 4.5.1 or lower (I think this may be related to #103310, which seemed to happen instead)

### System information

Godot v4.6.stable (89cea1439) - Windows - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility)

### Issue description

For each instance of a properly enabled `EditorExportPlugin`, if it supports the web platform, and at least one web export is set to runnable in the export options, all options retrieved (using `get_option`) in `_export_end()` (and __not__ `_export_begin()`) for all platforms will return the value set for the web platform instead of their respective platforms.

Regardless of weather or not you export a platform individually or all at once, and regardless of it's place on the list, the bug still occurs unless the web platform in not set to runnable

### Steps to reproduce

See below:

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

export_plugin.gd :
```
@tool
class_name WebOptionOverwriteBugExampleExportPlugin
extends EditorExportPlugin

func _get_name() -> String:
	return "WebBug2BugHarder"

func _supports_platform(platform:EditorExportPlatform):
	return not platform.is_class("EditorExportPlatformExtension")

func _get_export_options(platform):
	if not _supports_platform(platform):
		return []
	return [
		{
			"option" : {
				"name" : "bug_test/unique_example_string",
				"type" : TYPE_STRING,
			},
			"default_value" : "The default value doesn't seem effect this bug, only what the option is set for for the web platform will matter",
		}
    ]

func _export_begin(features:PackedStringArray, is_debug:bool, path:String, flags:int):
    print("Beginning it's export, the platform that exports to the path %s thinks that it's unique string in the following: '%s'" % [path, get_option("bug_test/unique_example_string")])

func _export_end():
    print("Ending it's export, the platform that exports to the path %s thinks that it's unique string in the following: '%s'" % [path, get_option("bug_test/unique_example_string")])
```

plugin.gd
```
@tool
extends EditorPlugin

var _current_inst:WebOptionOverwriteBugExampleExportPlugin = null

func _enter_tree():
	_try_init_plugin()

func _enable_plugin():
	_try_init_plugin()

func _disable_plugin():
	_try_deinit_plugin()

func _exit_tree():
	_try_deinit_plugin()

func _try_init_plugin():
	if _current_inst == null:
		_current_inst = WebOptionOverwriteBugExampleExportPlugin.new()
		add_export_plugin(_current_inst)

func _try_deinit_plugin():
	if _current_inst != null:
		remove_export_plugin(_current_inst)
		_current_inst = null
```

plugin.cfg
```
[plugin]

name="WebBugExample2"
description="Another plugin used to register a export plugin that shows off another bug when exporting to web"
author="NovaDC"
version="v0.0.0.0"
script="plugin.gd"
```

Do note that you must also set export options as indicated in the bug description to observe this.
